  ["real business activity/decision/effect/audit records for gftdcojp already live in orgs/gftdcojp/cloud-itonami (private, ADR-2606271700, closed) -- reconfirmed as the record of record, no relocation"
   "gftdcojp's own legal-entity identity record (LEI/legal-name/jurisdiction/website) reuses ADR-2607110300's cloud-itonami-lei-<LEI> schema and cloud-itonami org placement, but repo creation is BLOCKED until gftdcojp obtains a real GLEIF-issued LEI -- none exists in this workspace as of 2026-07-14, and fabricating one violates ADR-2607110300's own no-fabrication discipline"
   "etzhayyim and kotoba-lang are ruled out for both layers, same reasoning as ADR-2607110300 (etzhayyim = non-profit self-sovereign religious layer, out of scope for commercial entity records; kotoba-lang = language/infra layer, not a home for business entity content)"
   "activity data (private) and identity data (public) stay in separate repos/orgs, never mixed in one repo -- avoids accidentally leaking private activity content into a public identity archive"
   "LEI acquisition itself (GLEIF-accredited LOU application, KYC, fee) is a real-world legal-entity action outside standing agent authorization -- owner must execute it; agent proceeds with identity-repo scaffold only after a real LEI is on file"]
